  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-states",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "popup",
      "text": "Nine popup states, 360px wide.\nEvery artboard has a Dark tweak above it.\n\nCopy is real, not lorem \u2014 it is the copy the slices ship."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-gate",
      "x": 1760,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "popup",
      "text": "The four gated states.\n\nAds stay visible in all of them \u2014 enforcement-contract.md keeps the list ungated because a locked button beside your own ad is the conversion surface."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-402",
      "x": 2640,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 400,
      "page": "popup",
      "text": "Dunning, not \"lapsed\".\n\nADR-0018 sends a cancelled customer back to Free, so 402 now only ever means a card that is failing. Hence \"update your card\", never \"resubscribe\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-web",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -140,
      "w": 460,
      "page": "web",
      "text": "No login anywhere on these pages (ADR-0017).\n\nStripe lands on Success; the webhook does the real work, so the page never learns who anybody is. Privacy and Terms are what the Web Store listing requires."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-legal",
      "x": 960,
      "y": -140,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "web",
      "text": "The legal copy is structure plus an honest description of what AdBump does \u2014 marked [PLACEHOLDER]. It needs a lawyer before T58."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-tokens",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -130,
      "w": 440,
      "page": "tokens",
      "text": "This is what T28 (packages/ui) encodes.\n\nEvery value is lifted verbatim from the POC popup, so the design is continuous with what already ships. Two additions are called out on the sheet."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "popup"
  }
